# CryptoQuant

> CryptoQuant provides on-chain and market data, charts, analytics tools and research for crypto market analysis. Analysts, traders, developers and institutions use these resources to study blockchain activity and market conditions.

## Core uses

- Explore exchange flows, network activity and market indicators by asset.
- Compare metrics with price, build dashboards and configure alerts.
- Query data, investigate address cohorts and read analyst research.
- Integrate documented data endpoints into applications or connect an MCP client.

## Analytics Suite

- [Charts](https://cryptoquant.com/asset/btc/summary): Chart any on-chain metric against price by asset, exchange and time window.
- [Dashboards](https://cryptoquant.com/community/discover): Combine charts into boards that track exchange reserves, netflows and market trends in one view.
- [Alerts](https://cryptoquant.com/alert/preset): Preset and custom alerts delivered to email and Telegram.
- [Data API](https://docs.cryptoquant.com/guides/quickstart): Retrieve on-chain and market data through the CryptoQuant API.
- [SQL Queries](https://cryptoquant.com/analytics/query/create): Query raw blockchain data and CryptoQuant metrics directly, then publish the result as an indicator.
- [Pro Charts](https://cryptoquant.com/prochart/shared): TradingView-style charting with on-chain indicators overlaid on derivatives price action.
- [Cohorts](https://cryptoquant.com/analytics/query/create): Group addresses by balance, age or activity and track each cohort's holdings over time.
- [AI Assistant](https://cryptoquant.com/labs/chat): Ask on-chain questions in plain language and get charts and deeper insights back.
- [Indicator Heatmap](https://alpha.cryptoquant.com): See every on-chain indicator for an asset against price in a single view.
- [Analyst Consensus](https://consensus.cryptoquant.com): Daily analyst sentiment with the top analysts and their original calls.
- Alpha Builder (coming soon): Build, backtest and optimise strategies on CryptoQuant data.
- [MCP Server](https://cryptoquant.com/mcp): Connect compatible AI clients to CryptoQuant data using the Model Context Protocol. See the setup guide for access requirements and supported tools.

AI Assistant currently links to the development environment; access restrictions apply.

## Research and insights

- [Quicktakes](https://cryptoquant.com/insights/quicktake): Short-form market observations and on-chain analysis.
